1
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:09,960
They could be the hottest accessory of an even hotter summer.

2
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:20,990
As temperature records were smashed across Europe and other parts of the world, portable electric fans could be seen in the hands of millions of people.

3
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:27,380
Estimates claim that up to 8 million of these devices were sold in the UK alone.

4
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:35,220
The breeze that they provide will have been welcome to many, but could there be a downside to this popular product?

5
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:41,130
Concerns have been raised that these fans are just another example of fast technology.

6
00:00:41,130 --> 00:00:47,100
That is products that are sold cheaply and are likely to be disposed of quickly.

7
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:59,290
Research from Material Focus, a British pro-recycling organisation, suggests that half of all the mini fans bought will end up unused or thrown away.

8
00:00:59,290 --> 00:01:07,000
This is unsurprising as they can be cheap to buy and almost impossible to repair.

9
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:18,030
Fans contain a mix of different materials – plastic casing, copper wiring and a lithium-ion battery among other components.

10
00:01:18,030 --> 00:01:28,910
This means that a considerable amount of natural resource is used in their production, and that they can be complex to recycle and dispose of sustainably.

11
00:01:28,910 --> 00:01:33,010
There are more immediate safety risks from portable fans.

12
00:01:33,010 --> 00:01:43,410
The London Fire Brigade has reported cases of cheaply-made portable fan batteries catching fire or exploding while being charged.

13
00:01:43,410 --> 00:02:00,010
Waste disposal companies in the UK have warned that the lithium-ion batteries used by these devices are often thrown away together with household waste, and that this can lead to fires which put staff and installations at risk.

14
00:02:00,010 --> 00:02:03,020
It's not just fire either.

15
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:11,550
The Japanese Consumer Affairs Agency reports a train passenger's hair being sucked into someone else's fan on a train.

16
00:02:11,550 --> 00:02:20,150
In addition, once the air around you gets hot enough, fans can even make you warmer rather than colder.

17
00:02:20,150 --> 00:02:27,940
As the world's climate continues to heat up, more and more of us may be tempted to reach for portable fans.

18
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:35,960
But maybe we should take some time to reflect on the effect this might be having on our environment and climate.
